// @emit-error emitProgram: only i32 / boolean / string / array struct fields are supported
// A `u8[]` STRUCT FIELD IS NOT LOWERED YET, and this file exists to keep that refusal
// LOUD. It is the difference between a missing feature and a miscompile.
//
// The packed byte list ships for the VALUE positions — local, parameter, return, binding,
// global, closure capture — which is what `std:fs` needs. The CONTAINER positions (struct
// field, map value, ref-list element / `u8[][]`, the `T[] | null` niche) each have their
// own parallel kind ladder that has not been taught the packed backing, and a `u8[]` in
// one of them declines rather than falling through to a neighbouring rep.
//
// The fall-through it declines from is exactly the hazard: without the refusal a `u8[]`
// field took `fieldCodeOfSpelling`'s `return 5` (a REF list) and the emitter interned a
// ref-list wrapper for a one-byte backing — measured on the parent commit as a module
// that fails to parse, with `vl check` rc 0.
//
// THE SAME FIELD HAS A SECOND SPELLING, and it pins this exact sentence in
// `generics/error-u8-field-through-generic-alias.vl`: `type Box<T> = { v: T }` at
// `Box<u8[]>` reaches a DIFFERENT interner (`gaeEnsure`, not `collectS`), and until #1829
// that one read the same -1 and returned quietly — check-clean invalid wasm on the program
// this file refuses in one line. The two files must keep agreeing word for word; that they
// did not is what the drift was.
type S = { b: u8[] }
const s: S = { b: [3] }
print(s.b[0])
